{
  "set": "kernel/public/v1/weighted-draw",
  "kernelVersion": 1,
  "spec": "SuperEngine fairness kernel, kernelVersion 1: WeightedDraw, drawAlgorithmVersion 1",
  "description": "WeightedDraw(seed, weights) = (index, r, ctr), drawAlgorithmVersion 1, the draw over a book table's weights in table order. Checks, in order: seed is 32 bytes (else seed-length); at least one weight (else weights-empty); at most 2^32 weights (else weights-too-many); every weight is 0 to 2^64 - 1 (else weight-out-of-range); then the total W of the weights is at least 1 (else weight-total-zero) and at most 2^63 (else weight-total-too-large). Then (r, ctr) = Uniform(seed, W): limit = 2^256 - (2^256 mod W), and for ctr = 0, 1, 2, ...: x = uint256(keccak256(abi.encode(bytes32(\"draw-v1\"), seed, uint256(ctr)))), the hash of three 32-byte words in that order: the label's bytes zero-padded on the right, the seed, then ctr big-endian; keccak256 is Ethereum's Keccak-256, not NIST SHA3-256. The first x < limit gives r = x mod W and acceptedAtCtr = ctr. index is the 0-based row whose interval [cumulativeStart, cumulativeStart + weight) holds r, where cumulativeStart is the sum of the weights before the row, so a row of weight 0 is never drawn",
